comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-09T11:20:17.021Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict complete 2908-item all-status corpus and request-specific stdin/custom-field search, open and in-progress inventories checked. Full live metadata and history read for closed pm-kipd, pm-qvdj, pm-2589e6 and pm-field-key-recovery. Those delivered full-item transport, extension setters, annotation integrity and rejected-key diagnostics; none owns this schema/extension custom-field transport defect. Reproduced with independent disposable tracker: init, schema add-field escape_class --type string --commands create,update,list,search,context, then stdin document versus explicit --escape-class. JSON stderr exit 2 names key; explicit create exits 0. This follow-up remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-09T11:25:22.007Z","harness:codex",Registered the completed full-item transport seed pm-kipd with the existing CLI/SDK/MCP contract-drift family so this recorded recurrence inherits mandatory static/coverage admission. Registration selects protections and does not assert the schema/extension transport defect is fixed. Item remains open and unclaimed.
  "2026-10-09T11:52:53.835Z","harness:codex","Graph admission: inspection of the already completed rejected-field diagnostic exposed that the stdin adapter supplies a generated key assignment instead of the actual schema field. Reuse its diagnostic lineage; the new transport defect remains open and unclaimed."
